Fix item 4: make the strong baselines genuinely reachable by the search

Two defects in the first v2 campaign, both of which made item 4 untested:

1. extend_pool() appended RIEM/FB members without registering their feature
   types on the pool, and _pick_family() draws the family from
   pool.feature_types. No RIEM or FB member was selectable: 0 of 32 topologies
   contained one, so V4 was V0 plus 21 dead pool entries.

2. What was added were cousins of the strong baselines, not the baselines. B5
   runs on unfiltered epochs with a logistic-regression head; the members were
   band-passed with SVM heads. B4 (EEGNet) was not representable at all.

Adds a RAW view so a whole model can be a pool member, RiemannianExactNode
(verified to reproduce B5: 0.767 vs 0.767 on subject a / seed 42) and
EEGNetNode (with the softmax head EEGNetClassifier lacks). Both share the
STRONG family, so a committee can be a committee of strong baselines.

V4_enriched_pool now embeds the exact B5; new opt-in V7_strong_members adds
EEGNet. The EEGNet node is code-reviewed but unexecuted - torch was not
available in the authoring environment.

README_v2 records the campaign-1 result: none of the six changes improved on
the published method, and the method's own run-to-run variability (SD 17 points
per unit) exceeds every measured effect.
